## The split, stated before the test list

The PRD tags every criterion [auto], [static] or [manual], and the plan's TDD
routing names the four automated ones — AC-4 to AC-7 — as the pure `src/shared`
contracts this suite encodes. `documentation/40-engineering/testing-strategy.md`
keeps UI and chrome verification manual, and `docs/context/methodology.md` turns
that into an obligation rather than an exemption: the decidable part is
extracted and tested first; the glue and the assets are verified by the plan's
own VALIDATE probes (JSON parsed, pixels decoded, font bytes and gzip weights
measured) and, for the playground, by the browser pane. That is why the
[static]/[manual] rows above map to plan commands rather than to test files —
the same shape unit 2's phase-4 manifest used for its DOM half, approved then.

## Test files written this session

- `test/format.test.ts` — 27 cases in six `describe` blocks against the new
  pure `src/shared/format.ts` (plan Task 2, AC-A2 / AC-A3):
  - **`formatRemaining`** — zero special-cased to `{ figure: null, label:
    "nenhuma restante" }` (the case a `PluralRules`-driven label fails, because
    CLDR maps 0 to `one` for pt-BR); `1` singular; `2`, `4`, `12` plural with
    the figure as a string.
  - **`formatDayShort`** — `sex., 21/08`, `ter., 18/08`, the diacritic in
    `sáb., 22/08`, zero-padding in `dom., 04/01`, a regex pinning "three
    letters, exactly one period, comma, dd/mm" over four more days, and a
    year-end day (`qui., 31/12`).
  - **`formatHeaderDate`** — the default zone (`15:00Z` on the 21st →
    `sex., 21/08`), the timezone case that discriminates a UTC implementation
    (`01:00Z` on the 22nd is still `sex., 21/08` in São Paulo) and an explicit
    `"UTC"` argument giving `sáb., 22/08`.
  - **`taskMetaLine` — deadlines** — overdue with the short day, `ontem`,
    `até hoje` (not overdue), `até amanhã`, a later day, and `amanhã` / `ontem`
    computed across a month boundary (`2026-08-31` → `2026-09-01`).
  - **`taskMetaLine` — scheduled dates** — `atrasada · era para …`, `ontem`,
    `fazer hoje`, `fazer amanhã`, `fazer sáb., 29/08`, and `amanhã` across a
    year boundary.
  - **`taskMetaLine` — priority and closed Tasks** — ` · alta` / ` · baixa`
    appended, nothing for `normal`, the overdue flag preserved under a priority
    word, the bare word for an undated Task, `null` for an open undated Task
    with `null`/`normal` priority, `null` for any `done` Task (even an overdue
    high-priority one), and `{ text: "não concluída", overdue: true }` for a
    `missed` Task with nothing appended.
- `test/connectivity.test.ts` — 16 cases in four `describe` blocks against
  the new pure `src/shared/connectivity.ts` (plan Task 3, AC-A4): every
  browser event from every state (`it.each` over the three states), the
  request outcomes (`server-unreachable` from `online` and from
  `unreachable`; **`offline` winning over a `server-unreachable` failure** —
  the case a "last event wins" reducer fails; `http-error` leaving every
  state unchanged; `request-succeeded` from every state), three sequences the
  banner will see (airplane mode → failed refetch → reconnect → success;
  server down and back; a 4xx after reconnecting not faking an outage), and
  `canWrite` true for `online` only.

