## Why this suite is legitimately RED before implementation

Two different reds, both for the right reason:

- `test/format.test.ts` and `test/connectivity.test.ts` fail to load —
  `Cannot find module '../src/shared/format'` /
  `'../src/shared/connectivity'` — because the modules are created by plan
  Task 2 and Task 3. For brand-new pure modules that is the only red
  available; what carries the discrimination once they exist is the content
  of the assertions named above (zero-in-singular, the São Paulo timezone
  case, the month/year boundaries, `offline` winning, `http-error` being
  inert, `done` → `null`).
- The two updated cases are a **behavioural** red: `src/shared/request-failure.ts`
  and `src/shared/token-store.ts` still carry the English sentences, so the
  Portuguese `toBe` / `toThrow` assertions fail against real code until plan
  Task 4 translates them. The other 219 cases of the corpus stay green.

No test asserts on an invented internal, a private field or a call count. No
mock is used: the modules are pure, so the tests call them directly with plain
values; `now` and `today` are arguments, so no clock is faked.

